WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.243 --> 00:00:23.741
"This is so embarrassing," Iris thought as she missed another ball that Jae lobbed her way.

2
00:00:23.742 --> 00:00:28.998
She wished she had paired up with Javier—or anyone else.

3
00:00:28.999 --> 00:00:34.918
"I probably just need to warm up a little," she called to Jae with a nervous laugh.

4
00:00:34.919 --> 00:00:43.185
She exhaled and tried to relax. She took another swing. Another miss.

5
00:00:43.186 --> 00:00:47.909
"Or maybe this racket has a hole in it!" she joked.

6
00:00:47.909 --> 00:00:57.983
"Could be." Jae shrugged and hit another ball to her. Iris swung—and missed again.

7
00:00:57.984 --> 00:01:05.825
Jae scratched his head. "Didn't you say your soccer team made it to the state playoffs?"

8
00:01:05.826 --> 00:01:14.299
"The key word there is soccer," Iris said. "And trust me, tennis is nothing like soccer."

9
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:21.458
She looked down and inspected her racket. "Maybe I need a different one of these."

10
00:01:21.459 --> 00:01:29.029
"Having a problem over here?" Trent appeared from behind Iris, making her jump.

11
00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:38.696
"A problem? Uh . . ." Iris didn't know what to say. Instinctively, she glanced over at Javier.

12
00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:48.192
He was swinging his racket like crazy but not coming any closer to hitting the ball than she was.

13
00:01:48.193 --> 00:01:55.093
Trent followed her gaze. "You and Javier have never played tennis before, have you?"

14
00:01:55.094 --> 00:02:04.190
"Nope," Iris said. "Not even table tennis!" She grinned at Jae, and he chuckled.

15
00:02:04.191 --> 00:02:09.925
"It's okay." But Trent was frowning like it really wasn't okay.

16
00:02:09.926 --> 00:02:18.752
"Jae, why don't you partner up with Zoe instead?" He pointed at the blond girl hitting balls at Javier.

17
00:02:18.753 --> 00:02:26.316
Zoe heard Trent and turned to face them. Her face was already lit up into a smile.

18
00:02:26.317 --> 00:02:29.059
"Great idea!" she called.

19
00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:34.895
Jae flashed Zoe a grin. "Sure," he said. "Sounds good."

20
00:02:34.895 --> 00:02:40.583
Iris felt a flush creep up her face. Zoe was very pretty.

21
00:02:40.584 --> 00:02:48.481
Jae seemed very happy to be Zoe's partner, and Zoe looked just as happy to be partners with him.

22
00:02:48.482 --> 00:02:55.131
"You two can start practicing," Trent said to them. Then he waved Javier over.

23
00:02:55.132 --> 00:03:04.124
"I know Julie said we'd figure out the groups after tryouts, but there's no sense in keeping the two of you here.

24
00:03:04.125 --> 00:03:12.030
You really need to learn the basics of tennis first. Besides, the other group has fewer kids."

25
00:03:12.031 --> 00:03:18.283
He pointed to another court, where Ally stood observing the younger campers.

26
00:03:18.284 --> 00:03:27.038
"Just head on over there, and tell Ally I sent you." He turned back to the rest of the older group.

27
00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:33.188
Iris blinked. Trent had just sent them down to the baby class!

28
00:03:33.189 --> 00:03:38.679
She inspected her racket once more before following Javier off the court.

29
00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.338
Her brother didn't seem to be bothered in the slightest.

30
00:03:42.339 --> 00:03:47.426
Of course, he wasn't used to excelling at sports like Iris was.

31
00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:52.589
And this was about more than tennis. Jae was cute.

32
00:03:52.590 --> 00:04:01.733
She wanted to be in his group. So Iris had to learn how to play tennis—and learn fast.

33
00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:08.218
Ally saw Iris and Javier approaching. "What's up?"

34
00:04:08.219 --> 00:04:12.986
"Trent sent us to join your group," Iris mumbled.

35
00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:16.924
"We've never played tennis before," Javier said.

36
00:04:16.924 --> 00:04:20.263
"Oh, that's fine," Ally said.

37
00:04:20.263 --> 00:04:26.561
"His group had too many kids anyway, and we can definitely teach you some stuff over here."

38
00:04:26.562 --> 00:04:30.558
She waved at some kids who were playing on the court.

39
00:04:30.559 --> 00:04:35.301
Grace! Ben! Can you come over here for a minute?"

40
00:04:35.302 --> 00:04:49.628
Grace and Ben each stood about a head shorter than Iris, and their identical blond hair and blue eyes made them seem like polar opposites of Iris and Javier.

41
00:04:49.629 --> 00:04:55.902
"Twins?" All four kids blurted out the word at the same time.

42
00:04:55.903 --> 00:05:02.770
Ally laughed. "Yes! The four of you will be perfect teammates."

43
00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:11.769
Iris smiled as politely as she could, but the idea that these kids were her new teammates was kind of insulting.

44
00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:14.575
They looked about nine years old.

45
00:05:14.576 --> 00:05:19.085
Grace smiled at Iris. "Do you want to come with me?"

46
00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:23.429
Iris shrugged. "I guess," she mumbled.

47
00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:27.510
"So I must be with you," Javier said to Ben.

48
00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:33.347
Iris stared at her brother. He was giving the younger boy a friendly smile.

49
00:05:33.348 --> 00:05:43.320
"Javier seriously doesn't care that we're stuck playing with these little kids!" Iris thought. "Why isn't he embarrassed?"

50
00:05:43.321 --> 00:05:51.159
"Grace and Ben went to our junior camp last year," Ally said. "They won the final match for their age group."

51
00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:55.262
"Wow," Javier said. "Cool."

52
00:05:55.263 --> 00:06:00.399
Iris swallowed. "Great," she thought.

53
00:06:00.399 --> 00:06:07.487
Not only were they stuck with these babies, but these babies actually knew how to play tennis!

54
00:06:07.488 --> 00:06:13.319
Grace led Iris to an empty space on the court.

55
00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:18.451
"You guys must be pretty bad if they sent you down to our group!" she joked.

56
00:06:18.452 --> 00:06:25.474
"We've never played before, that's all," Iris said. "Once I learn what to do, I'll be fine."

57
00:06:25.475 --> 00:06:31.449
"Well, don't worry." Grace smiled. "Ally's a great coach."

58
00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:40.600
Ally jogged over to them. "First things first," she said. "Let me see your swing, Iris."

59
00:06:40.601 --> 00:06:47.374
Iris gripped the racket in both hands and gave it a powerful swing.

60
00:06:47.375 --> 00:06:52.765
"Uh-uh." Grace shook her head. "You're doing it all wrong."

61
00:06:52.765 --> 00:06:54.554
Iris flushed.

62
00:06:54.555 --> 00:07:01.855
"Here, watch me," Ally said. She planted her own feet hip-width apart.

63
00:07:01.855 --> 00:07:08.337
With one hip facing the net, she held her racket gently with both hands.

64
00:07:08.338 --> 00:07:16.751
When she swung, she shifted her weight gracefully toward the net, almost as though she was dancing with her racket.

65
00:07:16.752 --> 00:07:24.830
"So that's how you swing," Ally went on, "but you also have to pay attention to the ball."

66
00:07:24.831 --> 00:07:30.982
She tossed a tennis ball up in the air and caught it with the same hand.

67
00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:36.971
"Get ready, toss the ball, shift your weight, and swing!"

68
00:07:36.972 --> 00:07:42.739
Her racket struck the ball and lobbed it a few feet in front of her.

69
00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:48.736
"Maybe Iris should just focus on her swing for now," Grace suggested.

70
00:07:48.737 --> 00:07:54.662
"Sure," Ally said. "Good idea, Grace. I need to check on Javier."

71
00:07:54.663 --> 00:08:07.295
For the rest of the morning, Grace gave Iris tips as Iris practiced her swing and hit the ball against a practice wall.

72
00:08:07.296 --> 00:08:15.947
She made some slow progress, but there was a lot to remember, and they hadn't even started to play against each other yet!

73
00:08:15.948 --> 00:08:19.778
"Lunchtime!" Ally called.

74
00:08:19.779 --> 00:08:26.196
"Phew!" Iris thought. "Practice is finally over."

75
00:08:26.197 --> 00:08:36.875
She let out a sigh and followed Grace to the shady picnic tables where they'd all left their backpacks and lunches that morning.

76
00:08:36.876 --> 00:08:39.639
Jae was standing near her stuff.

77
00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:47.109
Iris' heartbeat sped up. They were in different groups now, but maybe they could still be friends.

78
00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:51.672
Before she could call out to him, he smiled at Zoe.

79
00:08:51.673 --> 00:08:53.970
"Ready?" he asked her.

80
00:08:53.971 --> 00:08:57.012
"Ready!" Zoe replied.

81
00:08:57.012 --> 00:09:12.930
Jae glanced quickly in Iris' direction, as if he knew she was there. But instead of saying anything to her, he simply looked away.
